  "issue": 325,
  "request": "Issue #325: 59de: [BUG] After task decomposition, implement/review/gate are not scoped to individual tasks\n\nBackground: In Issue #321, tasks[] was decomposed into T-1 through T-7, but implementation proceeded with currentTaskId null. review/gate-impl targeted the entire diff and all requirements, causing input overflow and long-running loops.\n\nExpected improvements: make currentTaskId mandatory during implementation when tasks[] exists; scope implement/review/gate-impl to the current task requirements and files; manage cursor advancement after task completion; prohibit broad gate with currentTaskId null or require explicit opt-in; treat full gate as a separate final step; include per-task implementation and verification results in final report.\n\nAcceptance criteria: implement/review/gate-impl without currentTaskId fails in task-decomposed flow; gate-impl input is limited to current task scope; CLI output explicitly shows how to advance after task completion; bulk implementation is recorded as explicit broad mode.",
